% generated-code-download — export generated code as a standalone TypeScript module

# Module: generated-code-download

Create a dependency-free TypeScript browser utility exporting exactly
`toGeneratedTypeScriptModule(source, exportName?)` and
`downloadGeneratedTypeScript(source, filename?, exportName?)`.

The first function MUST losslessly embed any non-empty source string (HTML, CSS,
JavaScript, backticks, and Unicode included) in a self-contained `.ts` module as
both a named constant and default export. Validate the export name as a valid
TypeScript identifier. Use JSON.stringify or an equivalent lossless escape.

The download function MUST use a UTF-8 TypeScript Blob and browser anchor
download flow, append `.ts` when missing, revoke the object URL after clicking,
reject empty input, and fail clearly outside a browser. Do not mutate source,
make network requests, or introduce dependencies.
